NAME
       fsck.xfs - a stand-in that does nothing for xfs file systems

SYNOPSIS
       fsck.xfs DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       fsck.xfs exists so that fsck and the boot process find a checker for
       xfs. It does nothing and succeeds: xfs keeps a journal and replays it
       when the file system is mounted, so it needs no check at boot.

       To check or repair an xfs file system, unmount it and use xfs_repair
       (xfs_repair -n only reports).

EXAMPLES
           umount /data
           xfs_repair /dev/vgdata/lvdata

SEE ALSO
       xfs_repair(8), fsck(8), xfs(5)
